{"id":1256,"date":"2020-11-25T19:49:11","date_gmt":"2020-11-26T03:49:11","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1256"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:45","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:45","slug":"build-the-crab-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-crab-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Crab Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4c909\" name=\"6a22164f4c909\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the base<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Built 4 7-hole metal frames to one blueboard. The two frames at the top will be at an angle!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt 2 4-hole metal frames three rows up from the bottom of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1257&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4ca57\" name=\"6a22164f4ca57\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the base: Part 2<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt a long L-frame to the center of the blueboard. The short side should be on the blueboard and the long side should be perpendicular to it.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a short L-frame above each of the 4-hole metal frames.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1258&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1259&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4cac7\" name=\"6a22164f4cac7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the legs: Part 1<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt a 4-hole metal frame between each set of 7-hole metal frames. They should be bolted on the third hole in for each side.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a 10-hole metal frame to the end of each 4-hole metal frame.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt 7-hole metal frames between to attach the 10-hole metal frames to the middle 7-hole metal frames.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Note: you may need to adjust the angle of some of the metal frames to make these steps work![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1260&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1261&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4cb27\" name=\"6a22164f4cb27\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the claws<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt long L-frames to the end of each 10-hole metal frame. They should form a right angle with the 10-hole metal frames.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the claws to the 10-hole metal frames with 2 more 10-hole metal frames. Again, you may need to adjust the angles of your parts to make this happen!<\/li>\n<li>Attach long standoffs to each of the 7-hole metal frames.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1262&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4cb85\" name=\"6a22164f4cb85\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Give it power<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt a DC motor to the two short L-frames.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the battery box to the long L-frame in the center of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Fasten the wheel to the DC motor. The wheel will stay on without the black screw!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1263&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1264&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1265&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4cc37\" name=\"6a22164f4cc37\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Attach the Smart Inventor Board<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Use 4 short standoffs to make 2 stacked standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Attach each stacked standoff to the Smart Inventor Board. Pay attention to the placement!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the Smart Inventor Board to the top row of the blueboard. It should be positioned in the center between the claws.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1266&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1267&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1268&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4ccc5\" name=\"6a22164f4ccc5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Crab Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To wire your Crab Bot, make sure the Smart Inventor Board is facing you:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1269&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1270&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22164f4cd14\" name=\"6a22164f4cd14\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>How to operate the Crab Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Watch the video to see how the Crab Bot works![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=dyaI2ZWpoEo&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 Build the base [vc_column_text] Built 4 7-hole metal frames to one blueboard. The two frames at the top will be at an angle! Bolt 2 4-hole metal&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-crab-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1742,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2208,2172,2171],"class_list":["post-1256","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-crab-bot","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-crab","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1256","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1256\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":6622,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1256\/revisions\/6622"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1742"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1256"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1256"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1256"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}